 "how": "the lane's kinematic derivations, tested on main's own mode functions by quadrature and central differences (checks/physical_c8_modes.py, D1 to D7; checks/physical_c8_tick_higgs.py, K7 to K9): the bubble's average is (p^2/2) sum |Theta_c|^2 times the identity; for the weight exp(-2 pi N y r^2) the moments are <r^2> = 1/(4 pi N y) and <r^4> = 3/(16 pi^2 N^2 y^2); <psi_j, d_X psi_k> = i delta/(4y) and <psi_j, d_y psi_k> = 0 (4e-11); the part of d psi orthogonal to the modes has squared norm |d tau|^2/(8y^2); the frame's matrices are T6 under tau -> tau + 1 and sqrt(tau/|tau|) S6 under S (2e-15), whence the factor e^(i arg(tau + 1)/2) on the word of the act; on the act's axis the angle changes by -2 arg(tau + 1) and the connection's integral is i arg(tau + 1)/2, which cancels that factor; the retwisted modes have transitions independent of the Wilson line (8e-14); their connection is i [dX/(4y) + pi N (xi d eta - eta d xi)] (9e-9); a move of the Wilson line by 1/N is the clock or the shift with the gauge factors stated (4e-14); the orthogonal part of the derivative has squared norm |d tau|^2/(8y^2) + (pi N/y)|d xi + tau d eta|^2 with no cross term (1e-7); the three retwisting phases cancel in the balanced product; the curvature and the product connection follow by differentiation and addition",
 "note": "These are conditional kinematics of the declared embedding, as the lane says: they derive part of the kinetic prescription main had supplied (the relative spectrum along the act's axis), not a law joining different Wilson backgrounds.",
